  "semanticText": "# Catalog Clause\n\nValidates a document-owned, single-supplier catalog and stores immutable keyed quotes. `state` defaults to `/catalog`, and `quotes` to `/quotes`. The authored catalog supplies its positive revision, supplier ID, three-character currency and keyed items. The clause validates it once on initialization and requires the quote destination to be absent or an empty object then. Optional `offer` title, text and sections describe the offer.\n\nThe `quote` action takes a stable key, current `catalogRevision` and at least one line. A line selects an item and positive whole quantity. The item's optional quantity cap applies. Items price per unit or per selected hour. A required service date uses a valid calendar date. Hourly items require an allowed duration. Repeating the same item, date and duration inside a quote is rejected. The configured connection supplies workflow authority.\n\nA stored quote freezes the supplier, catalog revision and identity, currency, and each line's item name, optional description, selection and price. The clause stores line pricing, discounts and totals in minor units and sums the lines into quote totals. An existing quote key returns a duplicate for identical input and conflicts for different input. A new key must name the current catalog revision. If `quoteSnapshot` specifies additional document fields, `quoteSnapshots` must point to a separate collection for their keyed snapshots. A quote records price and selection. Booking, settlement and catalog replacement require their own workflow."
}
